# Opinion

Meeting: 0026-ensure-calendar-sync-basic-auth-and-cloud
Agent: ArchitectA
Task: ensure calendar sync basic auth and cloud
Context:
- Calendar web client must register basic-auth users locally, sync to configured cloud endpoint, and keep working when the remote store (e.g., Mongo) is unavailable.
- UX should surface sync state, expose a manual sync trigger, and continue to seed local demo data when remote services are down.
Position:
- A local-first model with scoped storage per user plus a pluggable remote adapter (Bearer or Basic) keeps the architecture simple and resilient.
- Sync status surfaced in the shell helps align expectations when remote connectivity or auth is missing.
Recommendations:
- Keep remote adapter auth-agnostic (scheme + optional verification) so server-side auth can evolve without client rewrites.
- Preserve clear separation between storage (local snapshot) and sync orchestration to keep failure modes contained.
- Continue prioritizing explicit status messaging over silent fallback to help users understand when cloud writes are deferred.
